# Byte-exact checkout, everywhere.
#
# Windows runner images set core.autocrlf=true, so a plain checkout rewrites LF to
# CRLF. That silently changes the bytes of hash-pinned artifacts: the F4c gate pins
# vendor/canonical_malbolge_py/malbolge.py by SHA-256, and on the first CI run with
# that oracle vendored it reported F4C_VENDORED_ORACLE_DRIFT (pinned e64af4f0...,
# found 4a2a666f...) because the runner had CRLF copies. An oracle whose bytes move
# under it is exactly the failure mode that hid the EOF bug, so no path in this
# repository is treated as text that git may re-endline.
* -text
